-- title:
--   Layer step for rational node rings with crossing presentation
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q\ge 5$, $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$. Further, $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element lying in $A$; write $A_{k_0}:=$ `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` for the induced valuation subring of $k_0$, and $\widehat{A_{k_0}}$ for its adic completion at its maximal ideal. The **base local hypotheses** require: $A_{k_0}$ is a discrete valuation ring, its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, it is a henselian local ring, its residue field is algebraically closed, and (`hκ`) every $a\in A$ admits $c\in k_0$ with $c\in A$, $a-c\in A$ and $a-c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$. The **layer family** consists of a type $\iota$, intermediate fields $K(n)$ of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$, each finite over $k_0$, valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K(n)$ characterised by $x\in A_n \iff x\in A$, and a base index $n_0$ with $K(n_0)\le K(n)$ for all $n$.
--
--   The field $F:=$ `fieldBar q M'` (an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, attached to level $q^2M'$ and the group `levelH q M'`) is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. The conclusion is asserted for all data satisfying the following groups of hypotheses.
--
--   **The level field $F_0$.** An intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subseteq F$ such that the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with $F_0$ is all of $F$, and such that (linear disjointness) for every finite extension $K'/k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $K'$-linearly independent family $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum of $k_0(K')$ and $F_0$ inside $F$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$.
--
--   **The valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$.** It satisfies: for $x\in k_0$, $x\in A$ iff the image of $x$ lies in $W_0$; $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; and its maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$.
--
--   **The node $O$.** A local noetherian subring $O$ of $F_0$ with $O\subseteq W_0$; for $x\in k_0$, $x\in A$ iff the image of $x$ lies in $O$; every $f\in O$ is congruent modulo non-units to a constant, i.e. there is $x\in k_0$ with $x\in A$, image in $O$, and $f-x$ not a unit of $O$; and $F_0$ is the fraction field of $O$ ($\forall f\in F_0$ there are $g,h\in O$, $h\ne 0$, with $fh=g$).
--
--   **The crossing presentation.** A natural number $E_0\ge 1$, the image $\pi_0\in O$, elements $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u\in O^{\times}$, a ring isomorphism $\iota_O$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto $\mathcal U:=$ `UVCrossingModel` $\widehat{A_{k_0}}\,(\pi_0^{E_0})$, that is $\widehat{A_{k_0}}[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^{E_0})$, and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of $\mathcal U$, subject to: $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$ in $O$; the constants law $\iota_O(x)=\mathrm{const}(x)$ for every $x\in k_0$ lying in $A$ and in $O$; $\iota_O(c_x)=\gamma_U\,U$ and $\iota_O(c_y)=\gamma_V\,V$; $c_y\in W_0$ and $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$; and $c_x$, whenever it lies in $W_0$, is not in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   **The Hasse germ.** The series `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q` lies in $F$; there are $a_0\in k_0$ with $J-a_0\in F_0$ (where $J$ denotes that element of $F$) and $J-a_0\in O$, an integer $e_J\ge 1$ and a unit $w_V$ of $\mathcal U$ with $\iota_O(J-a_0)=w_V\,V^{e_J}$.
--
--   **The chart of $O$.** A subring $B_x\subseteq O$ of $F_0$ such that $f\in O$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h\in O$, and such that $B_x$ is the subring generated by the images of the elements of $k_0$ lying in $A$ together with a finite set $T$.
--
--   **The first end $(R_x,b_x)$.** A field $FI$ over the residue field of $A$, a regular prolongation $R_x$ of $A$ to $F$ with residue field target $FI$ (a valuation subring `integers` of $F$ with a surjective residue homomorphism onto $FI$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$), and a place $b_x$ of $FI$ over the residue field of $A$, such that: $b_x$ is rational (the structure map to its residue field is surjective); $O$ is contained in $R_x$`.integers`; residues of elements of $O$ lie in the valuation subring of $b_x$; non-units of $O$ have residue in the maximal ideal of that valuation subring; $R_x.\mathrm{residue}(c_x)=0$; and $b_x.\mathrm{ord}(R_x.\mathrm{residue}(c_y))=1$.
--
--   **The second end $(R,n_d)$.** Likewise a field $FSS$ over the residue field of $A$, a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to $F$ with target $FSS$ and a place $n_d$, such that for $f\in F_0$ one has $f\in R$`.integers` iff $f\in W_0$; $n_d$ is rational; residues of elements of $O$ lie in the valuation subring of $n_d$ and non-units of $O$ land in its maximal ideal; $R.\mathrm{residue}(c_y)=0$; and $n_d.\mathrm{ord}(R.\mathrm{residue}(c_x))=1$.
--
--   **The place set $S$ and the node ring $\mathcal N$.** A set $S$ of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ characterised by: $P\in S$ iff the image of $O$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ and every non-unit $f$ of $O$ satisfies $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$ with value in the maximal ideal of $A$; all places in $S$ are rational. Further a subring $\mathcal N$ of $F$ with $f\in\mathcal N$ iff $f$ lies in $R_x$`.integers`, in $R$`.integers` and in the valuation subring of every $P\in S$; and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$ for $f\in\mathcal N$, $P\in S$.
--
--   **The constants and coefficient rings of the layers.** Subrings $C'(l)\subseteq A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, each a domain and a discrete valuation ring, with elements $\varpi'(l)\in C'(l)$; rings $W_c(l)$, each a domain, a discrete valuation ring and adically complete at its maximal ideal, with elements $\pi(l)$; natural numbers $e_L(l)$; and ring homomorphisms $j_c(l):C'(l)\to W_c(l)$, subject to: $c\in C'(l)$ iff $c\in A$ and $c$ lies in $K(l)$; for $d\in C'(l)$ the residue of $d$ in $A$ vanishes iff $d\in\varpi'(l)C'(l)$; $C'(n_0)\le C'(l)$; $\pi(l)$ is irreducible; $\pi_0=v\,\varpi'(l)^{e_L(l)}$ for some $v$ with $v,v^{-1}\in C'(l)$; $j_c(l)(\varpi'(l))=\pi(l)$; $j_c(l)$ reflects the powers of the uniformiser ($j_c(l)(c)\in(\pi(l)^n)\Rightarrow c\in(\varpi'(l)^n)$); and $j_c(l)$ has dense image ($\forall n,w\ \exists c$ with $w-j_c(l)(c)\in(\pi(l)^n)$).
--
--   **The layer and the base node ring.** A fixed index $l\in\iota$; the subring $\mathcal N_0$ of $F$ consisting exactly of the elements of $F$ that lie in $F_0$ and there in $O$, assumed local and noetherian; and a local noetherian subring $N_1$ of $F$ with $\mathcal N_0\le N_1$, satisfying: $N_1\le\mathcal N$; $S$ is exactly the set of places $P$ whose valuation subring contains $N_1$ and for which every non-unit $f$ of $N_1$ has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ in the maximal ideal of $A$; the image of $C'(n_0)$ lies in $N_1$; every $g\in N_1$ is congruent modulo non-units to a constant from $C'(n_0)$; linear disjointness over $C'(n_0)$ (for $C'(n_0)$-linearly independent $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,n\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,n\to N_1$, $\sum_i c_i\cdot a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$); the inclusion $\mathcal N_0\to N_1$ is local; $\mathfrak m_{N_1}\le \mathfrak m_{\mathcal N_0}N_1+(\varpi'(n_0))$; both reductions are regular and positive on non-units, i.e. for $f\in N_1$ in $R_x$`.integers` one has $b_x.\mathrm{ord}(R_x.\mathrm{residue}(f))\ge 0$, strictly positive if $f$ is a non-unit with non-zero residue, and likewise for $R$ and $n_d$; and $\mathrm{ringKrullDim}\,N_1\ge 2$. Finally a node chart for $N_1$ is assumed: a subring $B_x\subseteq N_1$ of $F$ containing the images of $c_x$, $c_y$ and $u$, such that $f\in N_1$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $N_1$ whenever $h\in N_1$, and $B_x$ is generated by the image of $C'(n_0)$ together with a finite set $T$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under all of the above there exists a subring $N_l$ of $F$, local and noetherian, such that:
--
--   1. $N_1\le N_l$;
--
--   2. if $l=n_0$ then $N_l=N_1$;
--
--   3. the inclusion $N_1\to N_l$ is local: a non-unit of $N_1$ remains a non-unit in $N_l$;
--
--   4. $N_l\le\mathcal N$;
--
--   5. $S$ is exactly the set of places $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose valuation subring contains $N_l$ and for which every non-unit $f$ of $N_l$ has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$ lying in the maximal ideal of $A$;
--
--   6. the image of $C'(l)$ lies in $N_l$;
--
--   7. every $g\in N_l$ is congruent modulo non-units to a constant from $C'(l)$: there are $o\in C'(l)$ with image in $N_l$ such that $g-o$ is not a unit;
--
--   8. linear disjointness over $C'(l)$: for $C'(l)$-linearly independent $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,n\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,n\to N_l$, $\sum_i c_i\cdot a_i=0$ implies all $a_i=0$;
--
--   9. $N_l$ carries a node chart: there is a subring $B_x\subseteq N_l$ of $F$ containing the images of $c_x$, $c_y$ and $u$, with $f\in N_l$ iff $f=g/h$ for some $g,h\in B_x$ with $h$ a unit of $N_l$ whenever $h\in N_l$, and $B_x$ is the subring generated by the image of $C'(l)$ together with a finite set $T$;
--
--   10. the images of $c_x$ and $c_y$ lie in $N_l$, and the image of $u$ lies in $N_l$ and is a unit there;
--
--   11. there are a ring homomorphism $\sigma:W_c(l)\to\widehat{N_l}$ into the adic completion of $N_l$ at its maximal ideal, and a ring isomorphism $\iota_c:\widehat{N_l}\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }$ `UVCrossingModel` $(W_c(l))\,(\pi(l)^{e_L(l)E_0})$, i.e. onto $W_c(l)[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi(l)^{e_L(l)E_0})$, such that:
--    (a) $\sigma(\pi(l))$ is the image of $\varpi'(l)$ in $\widehat{N_l}$, whenever that image lies in $N_l$;
--    (b) $\iota_c(\sigma(o))=\mathrm{const}(o)$ for all $o\in W_c(l)$;
--    (c) (Hasse germ) $J-a_0$ lies in $N_l$ and there are $e\ge 1$ and a unit $w$ of the crossing model with $\iota_c(J-a_0)=w\,V^{\,e}$;
--    (d) every $c\in C'(l)$ whose image lies in $N_l$ is in the image of $\sigma$: there is $o\in W_c(l)$ with $\sigma(o)$ equal to the image of $c$ in $\widehat{N_l}$;
--    (e) (first residue law) for $f\in N_l$ lying in $R_x$`.integers` with $R_x.\mathrm{residue}(f)\ne 0$ and $b_x.\mathrm{ord}(R_x.\mathrm{residue}(f))=n$, there is a unit $\gamma$ of the crossing model with $\iota_c(f)-\gamma\,V^{\,n}\in(\mathrm{const}(\pi(l)),U)$;
--    (f) (second residue law) for $f\in N_l$ lying in $R$`.integers` with $R.\mathrm{residue}(f)\ne 0$ and $n_d.\mathrm{ord}(R.\mathrm{residue}(f))=n$, there is a unit $\gamma$ of the crossing model with $\iota_c(f)-\gamma\,U^{\,n}\in(\mathrm{const}(\pi(l)),V)$.
--
--   Here `Place.ord` is the negative logarithm of the adic valuation of the place, `Place.IsRational` means surjectivity of the structure map onto its residue field, and `Place.evalAt` returns the residue-field value of an element of the valuation subring, read back in the base field, and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the single-layer step in the construction of the layered rational node rings attached to a node of the modular curve at full level: it transports a node ring defined over the base constants $C'(n_0)$ to a node ring over the constants $C'(l)$ of the $l$-th layer, preserving the crossing presentation of the completion (now of thickness $e_L(l)E_0$), the node chart, the germ of the $j$-expansion and the two residue laws at the two branches. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_layeredRationalNodeRings_of_node_ends_layers`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_layeredRationalNodeRings_of_node_ends_layers), which iterates it over all layers and identifies the $l=n_0$ case with the base ring.
